; The reserved demand__ prefix, CROSS-KIND (found by this corpus's expansion
; 2026-08-04, fixed same day): a user #local spelled exactly like the
; would-be fabricated demand MESSAGE (demand__<query>_<adorn>, same arity)
; must reject under -demand -- AddDecl enforces cross-kind (name,arity)
; uniqueness but fabrication bypasses AddDecl, so the G3 pre-check scans
; ALL declaration kinds. Compiles fine without -demand (.drflags carries it).
#message e_1(u64 X).
#local demand__q_b(u64 P).
demand__q_b(X) : e_1(X).
#local p(u64 A).
p(A) : e_1(A).
#query q(bound u64 A) : p(A).
